  {
    "episode_id": 90182,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90182.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "Sure. Well, thank you for having me on because I do think that doing things like this is a part of making sure that people are aware of a historical perspective and the importance of advocacy. So as the three of us know, this system has been underappreciated, undervalued and underfunded from state government for over a decade. And we were fortunate in my first year as disabilities chair to get a small percent cost of living adjustment. And then the significant one last year of 5.4 percent increase. We know that the challenges are great out there and our number one challenge is related to workforce. So we have to support our voluntary providers so that they can support their employees and make sure that they're providing them with a decent wage. So, you know, the budget is supposed to be completed by April 1st and here we are talking. in the middle of April.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
